---
// Who holds what: app, wallet, proof server, contract.
---
<figure class="dg not-content">
  <ol class="dg-row">
    <li class="dg-card">
      <span class="dg-zone">Your browser</span>
      <p class="dg-title">The app</p>
      <p class="dg-text">A static website. Shows your balances, checks the contract is immutable, and asks your wallet to send.</p>
      <p class="dg-note">Never sees your keys</p>
    </li>
    <li class="dg-card dg-card--shielded">
      <span class="dg-zone">Your control</span>
      <p class="dg-title">Your wallet</p>
      <p class="dg-text">Holds your keys, gets the proof made, pays the DUST fee, and submits the transaction.</p>
      <div class="dg-sub dg-sub--warn">
        <p class="dg-title dg-title--sm">Proof server</p>
        <p class="dg-text">Makes the proof and sees key material. Local or remote: your wallet decides.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="dg-card">
      <span class="dg-zone">Midnight</span>
      <p class="dg-title">The contract</p>
      <p class="dg-text">Locks and releases NIGHT, and mints and retires sNIGHT.</p>
      <p class="dg-note">Immutable, no admin key</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>Requests flow from the app to your wallet to the network. Only your wallet, and the proof server it chooses, handle keys.</figcaption>
</figure>
